  "reason": "The study compares anatomical reorganization in primate brains (macaque, chimpanzee, human) using computational neuroanatomy and myelin-based cortical alignment. While it discusses evolutionary adaptations and differences in brain structure and connectivity, it does not report any quantitative measure of agreement between non-human animal results and human clinical results or a comparison of effect sizes. The focus is on understanding evolutionary changes in brain architecture, not on the predictive accuracy or concordance of animal models for human clinical outcomes."
